From 595689532dcbb252ab49f6f47678962d62734454 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <winshyon@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:30:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(data): soup data forge stops writing empty-answer rows
 for failed judge calls (#1221)

`soup data forge --judge-provider` built its judge without
`raise_on_error`, so every transport, HTTP or parse failure came back as
empty text. `score_uncertainty` rates an empty reply 1.0, so no
`--uncertainty-threshold` could prune it: the command wrote one
empty-assistant row per failed call, printed "synth complete" and
exited 0.

Build the forge judge with `raise_on_error=True` (as `soup data recipe`
does since #969). `synthesise_forge_rows` now takes an optional
`ForgeJudgeStats` and counts every call that raises, returns a malformed
reply or returns empty text as a failure instead of a row, whatever the
threshold. The CLI reports `N of M judge calls failed` with the
provider, endpoint and first error; it exits 1 without writing files when
no usable row was produced, and keeps the successful rows (with a
warning) on a partial outage.

Closes #1221
